      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>CHS Foundation has become an essential partner to enhance the extra programs and activities at Clairemont High. We support all CHS clubs athletics Circle of Friends academies classes VAPA the staff and much more. The Foundation works directly with CHS administration to make the best use of resources in order to make the most positive impact for all CHS students</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>School Club Support - Managed and safeguarded funds earned by school clubs ensuring teachers had quick and reliable access to their club earnings for student activities and supplies. Oversaw accurate financial accounting and coordinated support to maintain transparency efficiency and trust in the use of club-generated resources.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>114354</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>5k Fun Run - Led the annual 5K Fun Run as part of the Foundations ongoing initiative to strengthen connections among families school staff and the broader community. The event successfully raised funds to provide ten $250 teacher grants supporting classroom supplies and enhancing educational resources while promoting wellness and community engagement.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>2500</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>2083</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Spring Fling - Organized and executed the annual Spring Fling a community-building event designed to celebrate school staff and strengthen engagement among parents faculty and the broader Clairemont community. Coordinated attendance of approximately 250 participants including 50 school faculty members while raising funds to support school clubs and the Foundations continued initiatives. The event successfully fostered stronger community relationships and reinforced local support for educational programs.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>2500</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>2019</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
